  "PersonalityTraits": [
    "I always have an exit planned \u2014 and a second one, in case the first is on fire.",
    "I can\u0027t resist a locked box. Not to steal from, just to know."
  ],
  "Ideal": "Freedom. Chains are meant to be picked, and so are the people who make them.",
  "Bond": "My little brother Wim is apprenticed to a locksmith in Greyhaven. Everything I send home is so he never has to do what I do.",
  "Flaw": "I talk my way into trouble faster than I can sneak out of it.",
  "PortraitPath": null,
  "PlayerName": "",
  "Age": "24",
  "Height": "2\u002711\u0022",
  "Weight": "36 lb",
  "Eyes": "Hazel",
  "Skin": "Freckled tan",
  "Hair": "Curly auburn",
  "Gender": "Female",
  "Backstory": "Tam grew up on the barges of the Silverflow, running dice games and cons for her aunt\u0027s crew. When the crew sold a debtor to slavers, she picked the lock on his chains, sank the slavers\u0027 skiff, and has been working the other side of the law ever since \u2014 mostly.\n\nLevel 1: Signs on with a caravan heading upriver after a card game goes badly wrong in Greyhaven.\n\nLevel 3: Takes the Boots of Elvenkind off a smuggler who won\u0027t be needing them. Joins the Thieves\u0027 Guild of Rellport on probation \u2014 the guildmaster wants her fast hands for a job in the duke\u0027s vault.",
  "Allies": "Aunt Morra (estranged, still running the barge crew); Wim Underbough; Old Hobb the fence at the Crooked Kettle",
  "Treasure": "A marked deck of cards; a signet ring from the smuggler (whose house?); a map of the duke\u0027s cellars, half finished.",
